    "prompt": "I threw 9 coins into the air. If twice as many coins landed heads up as landed tails up, how many coins landed heads up?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Groups of three",
        "body": "For each coin that lands tails up, two land heads up, so the coins come in groups of 3 (1 tail, 2 heads). 9 coins make 3 groups, so there are $3 \\times 2 = 6$ heads.\n\n**Answer: (D) 6**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Make a list",
        "body": "Tails and heads: 1 and 2 (total 3), 2 and 4 (total 6), 3 and 6 (total 9). So 6 heads.\n\n**Answer: (D) 6**"
      }
    ],
